  "limitations": [
    "Mutation guard is controller-local, not cross-tab idempotency or session revocation detection.",
    "Draft/settings edits hide results but do not abort already dispatched mutations; navigation/unmount abort browser waiting, not kernel work.",
    "330-second mutations and 20-second inventory reads are active-browser bounds, including body reading; not a combined server pipeline deadline or proof of rollback.",
    "No automatic retry/detach or implicit local fallback is added by the browser. Existing guarded server Aya fallback remains unchanged.",
    "Only explicit clean true confirms cleanup. Ready inventory is a valid last response, not current global state or a server-side transaction snapshot.",
    "Explicit null bulk detach retains disclosed current-account-at-execution scope, including attachments added before execution.",
    "Synthetic fetch fixtures allow late continuations after cancellation; production tests use native fetch with mocked HTTP.",
    "Saved-script/template/learning refresh lifecycles and breakpoint event filtering are not fixed by this pass; supplementary learning reads are not newly race-free.",
    "Mock result display is not real kernel attach verification. Earlier full-backend/acceptance results are historical and not added."
  ],
